 "answer": {
  "answer": "The goal was met: five settings, each on a different scene, failed on every repeat (S1, S8, S16, S35, S41). None of these failures looks like a simulator artifact. All five pair a slowed recorded car (0.5x or 0.75x) with a faster ego at hand-off (1.2x or 1.4x), and four of them also have the car moved 1 to 2 s earlier. Each rests on only three runs, so the 90% range only just clears 0.5. They are confirmed as challenging, not measured precisely. Only two scenes fail in the way the brief pictured, with the ego running into a slow car ahead: 023b7fcc (S1) and 187e6244 (S35). In 187e6244 the policy took over about 1 s from impact, so it may not be the policy's fault. In the other three scenes (S8, S16, S41) the policy steered left into a car in the next lane, a car the study did not retime. That points to a lateral weakness in the policy, more than to the cut-in or lead-car timing.",
  "findings": [
   {
    "claim": "On 023b7fcc, with the lead car 2 s early at 0.5x speed and the ego at 1.2x, every run failed the same way. The policy barely braked as the gap to the slower lead car closed and hit it from behind. The policy was at fault.",
    "settings": [
     "S1"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "The S1 failure has a sharp edge. With the lead car only 1 s early or on time (other knobs the same), or at 0.75x speed with the ego at 1.4x, single runs passed. These are one run each, so they are hints, not rates.",
    "settings": [
     "S1",
     "S3",
     "S5",
     "S2"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 187e6244, with the car 1 s early at 0.5x and the ego at 1.4x, every run hit the slower lead car. But the policy took over with about 1 s to impact and braked only lightly, so the triage could not say whether the policy was at fault. The setup itself may have made the crash unavoidable.",
    "settings": [
     "S35"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 096988dd (car 2 s early, 0.75x, ego 1.4x), every run failed because the policy drifted left, against the route command, into a car passing in the next lane. The truck ahead played no part. With the car 1 or 1.5 s early instead, runs passed, including two repeats at 1 s.",
    "settings": [
     "S8",
     "S10",
     "S12"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 19f339ba (car 1 s early, 0.5x, ego 1.4x), every run failed the same way. The policy braked hard on an open highway for no visible reason, drifted left, and hit a car overtaking in the left lane. At 0.75x car speed, or with the car on time and the ego at 1.2x, single runs passed.",
    "settings": [
     "S41",
